# Context: create with getters

When calling `createX(...)` (from `createContext`), pass an **object with `get` accessors** for every field that comes from reactive props or load data. Do not snapshot values, and do not wrap the whole object in a thunk.

## Context module

```ts
import { createContext } from 'svelte';

export const [useMovie, createMovie] = createContext<Movie>();
```

Order is `[useX, createX]` (get, set).

## Setting context

```svelte
<!-- ✅ GOOD — getters keep reactivity across the context boundary -->
createMovie({
	get id() {
		return movie.id;
	},
	get title() {
		return movie.title;
	}
});

createApp({
	get user() {
		return data.user;
	},
	get isAuthenticated() {
		return data.user != null;
	}
});
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD — snapshots / breaks reactivity -->
createMovie(movie);
createApp({ user: data.user });
createApp(() => ({ user: data.user }));
```

## Reading context

```svelte
const movie = useMovie();
const app = useApp();
```

Children read fields from the context value (`movie.title`, `app.user`) — do not re-accept those fields as props when context already provides them.
